"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6042007238/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6062606577","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124228#issuecomment-6062606577","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124228","id":6062606577,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABaVwI8Q","user":{"login":"Delsin-Yu","id":71481700,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDgxNzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71481700?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu","html_url":"https://github.com/Delsin-Yu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-08T14:55:22Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T14:55:22Z","body":"<img width=\"981\" height=\"192\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/04cdb94b-cb5d-4dc5-a2a1-20609a64b4f1\" />\r\n\r\nOne thing that just came to mind, should we make the failing message more user-friendly? A user who writes non-unloadable code might not know what's causing it (or what a GC handle is, or when they spawned new threads), or even what an ALC is.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6062606577/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6063428737","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124228#issuecomment-6063428737","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124228","id":6063428737,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABaWiUgQ","user":{"login":"NoctemCat","id":22471296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDcxMjk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22471296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat","html_url":"https://github.com/NoctemCat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-08T15:34:57Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T15:34:57Z","body":"> One thing that just came to mind, should we make the failing message more user-friendly? A user who writes non-unloadable code might not know what's causing it (or what a GC handle is, or when they spawned new threads), or even what an ALC is.\r\n\r\nMaybe, but I don't know how to describe it better with less words, atm it's just moved straight from `Main.cs` `Console.Error.WriteLine(\"Failed to unload assemblies. Possible causes: Strong GC handles, running threads, etc.\");`, so it is already existing error message that is just moved to a more visible place. If the failing message become even bigger it would be too big.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6063428737/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6064755466","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124228#issuecomment-6064755466","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124228","id":6064755466,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABaXzTCg","user":{"login":"neikeq","id":7718100,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MTgxMDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7718100?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq","html_url":"https://github.com/neikeq","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-08T16:49:24Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T16:49:24Z","body":"Some suggestions:\r\n\r\nLong:\r\n\r\n```\r\nAssembly unload failed.\r\nThe previous assembly could not be unloaded and may remain in memory. This usually means some code is still holding a reference to it.\r\nThe new assembly was loaded successfully, so you can continue working normally. The leaked assembly will remain in memory until the process exits.\r\n```\r\n\r\nShort:\r\n\r\n```\r\nAssembly unload failed.\r\nThe previous assembly may remain in memory. The new assembly loaded successfully, so you can continue working normally.\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd maybe include the \"possible causes\" line as well.\r\n\r\nAlso, perhaps this shouldn't be a toast at all and just a warning/error in the Output panel instead. Something as aggressive as a toast might not be necessary now that things can continue working after an unload failure.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6064755466/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6065178347","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124228#issuecomment-6065178347","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124228","id":6065178347,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABaYNG6w","user":{"login":"NoctemCat","id":22471296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDcxMjk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22471296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat","html_url":"https://github.com/NoctemCat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/repos","ev